 Africa was born in war, has been cursed by crises and ruptures, and today stands on a precipice once again. This book explores the country's tumultuous journey from the Second Anglo-Boer War to 2021. Drawing on diaries, letters, oral testimony and diplomatic reports, Thula Simpson follows the South African people through the battles, elections, repression, resistance, strikes, insurrections, massacres, crashes and epidemics that have shaped the nation. Tracking South Africa's path from colony to Union and from apartheid to democracy, Simpson documents the influence of key figures including Jan Smuts, Nelson Mandela, Steve Biko, P.W. Botha, Thabo Mbeki and Cyril Ramaphosa. He offers detailed accounts of watershed events like the 1922 Rand Revolt, the Defiance Campaign, Sharpeville, the Soweto uprising and the Marikana massacre.","thumbnailUrl":"https://books.google.com/books/content?id=Fr-CEAAAQBAJ&printsec=frontcover&img=1&zoom=1&edge=curl&source=gbs_api","experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[{"name":"Nelson Mandela","confidence":0.82},{"name":"Jan Smuts","confidence":0.7}],"centralPlaces":[{"name":"South Africa","confidence":0.99}],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"South Africa’s transition from colony to democracy was shaped by recurring war, political crises, repression, resistance, and mass violence.","confidence":0.86},"academicOrientation":{"score":64,"confidence":0.82},"profileConfidence":0.91,"lowerConfidenceCandidates":{"centralFigures":[{"name":"Steve Biko","confidence":0.68}],"centralPlaces":[{"name":"Sharpeville","confidence":0.68},{"name":"Soweto","confidence":0.67}]},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"192448f357c8a51f7e571a33509e247b3a3534b6de53966c398b80c9843eee71","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"displaySummary":"This book explores the country's tumultuous journey from the Second Anglo-Boer War to 2021. Drawing on diaries, letters, oral testimony and diplomatic reports, Thula Simpson follows t